      },
      {
        "contentUdi": "umb://element/23c72b393bde4c5899d0b3917dfc70e0",
        "settingsUdi": "umb://element/266b8464a12c421f8b82d0c8825b72cb"
      }
    ]
  },
  "contentData": [
    {
      "caption": "Example application",
      "contentTypeKey": "bfeed15c-3ebb-46d4-b805-07d0f9b083c7",
      "udi": "umb://element/331c0b0e039a4a43841711de3b87a921"
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "394dc214-e2ad-4605-ab3f-2c6b83063ef6",
      "text": "",
      "udi": "umb://element/9ae2d25f0ce84944ba9834dfd3571626"
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "e0876897-88f4-4dcf-ae0a-ec5a37e3a185",
      "text": {
        "markup": "<p></p>\n<h2 class=\"govuk-heading-m\">Address lookup examples</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/{localLink:umb://document/7b185075ab794070b55b32b41d2d00e2}\">No data provided</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/{localLink:umb://document/520536163dc24233b9c308406775bc0e}\">Primary address data provided</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/{localLink:umb://document/773dac293a6c4938b7775ef9c877bbbf}\">Primary and secondary address data provided</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/{localLink:umb://document/801b1f274c4241d48e418f8e9ff00043}\">JavaScript disabled</a></li>\n</ul>",
        "blocks": {
          "contentData": [],
          "settingsData": []
        }
      },
      "udi": "umb://element/23c72b393bde4c5899d0b3917dfc70e0"
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "83cb35fb-51da-45cd-913f-1b8bdfd6a1d9",
      "iconFallbackText": "",
      "text": {
        "markup": "<p>This component relies on JavaScript to allow it's full functionality.</p>",
        "blocks": {
          "contentData": [],
          "settingsData": []
        }
      },
      "udi": "umb://element/08566006fde94f0b8d95dcad8ac18779"
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "e0876897-88f4-4dcf-ae0a-ec5a37e3a185",
      "text": {
        "markup": "<p>The address lookup component can be added to any page where you want the user to be able to search for an address.&nbsp;<br><br>Given a postcode and a building name or number the&nbsp;<a rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://www.ordnancesurvey.co.uk/products/os-places-api\" target=\"_blank\">Ordnance Survey Places API</a> is queried using the postcode endpoint. Results are then filtered by the building name or number. If an exact match is found, the user is taken to the 'confirmed' view. If more than one result is found, the user must select an address and is then taken to the 'confirmed' view.</p>\n<p>The 'confirmed' view populates hidden inputs with values, including the UPRN.</p>\n<p>The user also has the option to manually enter a UK or international address.</p>\n<p>The JavaScript file '<strong>address-lookup/index.js'&nbsp;</strong>is provided as part of the&nbsp;<strong>'ThePensionsRegulator.Frontend'</strong> NuGet package. This must be included in any view that uses this component.</p>",
        "blocks": {
          "contentData": [],
          "settingsData": []
        }
      },
      "udi": "umb://element/9b6733277a0144fe960be36d60e2d0a2"
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "40bb2a3e-3d75-4ec1-9134-e0c46c6f04a0",
      "text": {
        "markup": "<p>&lt;script src=\"_Content/ThePensionsRegulator.Frontend/tpr/address-lookup/index.js\" type=\"module\"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;</p>",
        "blocks": {
          "contentData": [],
          "settingsData": []
        }
      },
      "udi": "umb://element/981fce059fc54cec8b215aa27d95ec9c"
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "e0876897-88f4-4dcf-ae0a-ec5a37e3a185",
      "text": {
        "markup": "<p>If JavaScript is not available then the component will display input fields for entering an international address. The labels for these fields can be customised.</p>\n<p>Use the <strong>'tpr-address-lookup-legend'</strong> tag helper to add a legend to the fieldset. The legend will be rendered as a proper <code>&lt;legend&gt;</code> element with the <code>govuk-fieldset__legend</code> class applied.</p>\n<h2 class=\"govuk-heading-m\">Customising labels and error messages</h2>\n<p>Labels and validation error messages can be customised in three ways, listed here in priority order:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Server-rendered inputs</strong> \u2013 The component captures the label text, required message, max length, and pattern message from any <code>&lt;input&gt;</code> or <code>&lt;select&gt;</code> elements rendered inside the <code>&lt;tpr-address-lookup&gt;</code> element. These are used when JavaScript rebuilds the component. In Umbraco, configure these via the <strong>Address lookup</strong> content properties (e.g. Address line 1 label, Town or city label) and the <strong>Address lookup settings</strong> properties (e.g. Address line 1 error message required, Town or city error message maximum length).</li>\n<li><strong><code>data-*</code> attributes on the container</strong> \u2013 For fields that only exist in JavaScript (building name, UK postcode for the search view, county, and select address), you can set <code>data-address-lookup-{field}-{property}</code> attributes on the <code>&lt;tpr-address-lookup&gt;</code> element. In Umbraco, configure these via the corresponding <strong>Address lookup</strong> content properties (e.g. Building label, Postcode label, County label, Select address label) and <strong>Address lookup settings</strong> properties (e.g. Building error message max length, Postcode error message required, County error message maximum length, Select address error message required).</li>\n<li><strong>Built-in defaults</strong> \u2013 If no value is provided by either of the above methods, the component falls back to default values defined in <code>config.js</code>.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>The available <code>data-*</code> attributes for JavaScript-only fields are:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>data-address-lookup-postcode-label</code></li>\n<li><code>data-address-lookup-postcode-required</code></li>\n<li><code>data-address-lookup-postcode-maxlength</code></li>\n<li><code>data-address-lookup-postcode-pattern</code></li>\n<li><code>data-address-lookup-building-label</code></li>\n<li><code>data-address-lookup-building-maxlength</code></li>\n<li><code>data-address-lookup-county-label</code></li>\n<li><code>data-address-lookup-county-maxlength</code></li>\n<li><code>data-address-lookup-select-address-label</code></li>\n<li><code>data-address-lookup-select-address-required</code></li>\n</ul>",
        "blocks": {
          "contentData": [],
          "settingsData": []
        }
      },
      "udi": "umb://element/323d638c7e184b548ded29cc90343b3f"
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "40bb2a3e-3d75-4ec1-9134-e0c46c6f04a0",
      "text": {
        "markup": "<div>\"AddressLookup\": {</div>\n<div><span>&nbsp; &nbsp; \"SearchEndpoint\": \"https://api.os.uk/search/places/v1/postcode\",</span></div>\n<div><span>&nbsp; &nbsp; \"AddressByIdEndpoint\": \"https://api.os.uk/search/places/v1/uprn\"</span></div>\n<div>}</div>",
        "blocks": {
          "contentData": [],
          "settingsData": []
        }
      },
      "udi": "umb://element/c107320449354eef845b4772da6e6234"
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "5d33cd38-b819-4afd-9d4a-499ee73799ab",
      "udi": "umb://element/2a42c77d6d9447de8a1f538e6bfc4782"
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "83cb35fb-51da-45cd-913f-1b8bdfd6a1d9",
      "iconFallbackText": "",
      "text": {
        "markup": "<p>Consuming services must implement ITprCountryRepository to allow this components full functionality.</p>",
        "blocks": {
          "contentData": [],
          "settingsData": []
        }
      },
      "udi": "umb://element/dfa4b4c60d7249b89af1f785407b9bde"
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "e0876897-88f4-4dcf-ae0a-ec5a37e3a185",
      "text": {
        "markup": "<h2 class=\"govuk-heading-m\">Primary and secondary address lookup components</h2>\n<p>An address lookup component can be configured to be a primary or secondary component. It defaults to primary.</p>\n<p>If the component is configured to be secondary, a checkbox is displayed which, when checked, puts that component in the 'confirmed' view with the same address as the primary component.</p>\n<p>The secondary component expects the primary component to appear first on the page.</p>\n<h2 class=\"govuk-heading-m\">Configuration</h2>\n<p>Two URLs are required to be configured to allow this component to search for addresses.</p>\n<p><strong>SearchEndpoint</strong></p>\n<p>This should be the URL for the <a href=\"https://docs.os.uk/os-apis/accessing-os-apis/os-places-api/technical-specification/postcode\">postcode endpoint</a> of the Ordnance Survey API, or an equivalent service.</p>\n<p><strong>AddressByIdEndpoint</strong></p>\n<p>This should be the URL for the <a href=\"https://docs.os.uk/os-apis/accessing-os-apis/os-places-api/technical-specification/uprn\">UPRN endpoint</a> of the Ordnance Survey API, or an equivalent service.</p>\n<p>These are configured via the&nbsp;<strong>appsettings.json</strong> under a section named <strong>AddressLookup.</strong></p>",
        "blocks": {
          "contentData": [],
          "settingsData": []
        }
      },
      "udi": "umb://element/3a50bbe7809d45489fee38c5923efe25"
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "e0876897-88f4-4dcf-ae0a-ec5a37e3a185",
      "text": {
        "markup": "<p>To allow the 'manual international view' to show a select input of countries, consuming services must implement ITprCountryRepository.</p>",
        "blocks": {
          "contentData": [],
          "settingsData": []
        }
      },
      "udi": "umb://element/c982a90f9e7a46309b45aa0b26d4803d"
    }
  ],
